From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:23:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SECURITY-RESCAN-2: no Gmail connect, fetch or disconnect
 while viewing as someone

The Gmail routes mixed the real and the viewed identity. Connect and
callback are GETs, so even a read-only view replaced the viewed member's
stored Gmail access with the viewer's own mailbox; with writes on, fetch
used the viewed member's refresh token and disconnect deleted their link
while revoking the viewer's at Google. A mailbox link is a credential,
like an API token, so all four are refused during impersonation.

